---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import berklee_show from '../assets/cafe_show_labelled.png';
import live_1 from '../assets/live_show1.jpg'
import dyl_drums from '../assets/dyl_drums1.jpg'
import dyl_insnow from '../assets/self/dyl_insnow.jpg'
import nscc_group from '../assets/nscc_group_pic.jpg'
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import '../styles/reel-title.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About Me"
			description="Montreal-based software developer, musician, and visual artist."
		/>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="about-page">
			<header class="reel-title">
				<div class="reel-title-copy">
					<p class="kicker">Musician · Developer · Artist</p>
					<h1>About</h1>
				</div>
				<p class="logline">
					My story is one about stubbornly following your dreams, and having fun along the way.  
				</p>
			</header>

			<div class="about-content">
				<p>
					Hello! My name is Dylan, and I love to make stuff. I spent my early years performing in big bands, 
					jazz ensembles and studying music theory, culminating in attending my dream school, <strong>Berklee 
					College of Music</strong>. I was able to seriously improve my music writing, production and performance. 
					I met some unbelievably talented musicians who	I am priviledged to call friends. I also got to play 
					some <strong>incredible</strong> shows.
				</p>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={berklee_show}
						height={500}
						width={500}
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Playing a packed show with <strong>The Trap Music Orchestra</strong> at the Berklee Cafe.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={live_1}
						height={400}
						width={820}
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Cheesing with the crowd during a show in Hamilton, ON (<strong>thumbs up!</strong>)
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<p>
					After Berklee I played professionally for another 5 years in various bands and solo shows. Our 
					gigs included weddings, festivals, basements, backyards, theatres, clubs, and parties. The pay
					was terrible and I was having the time of my life. I got to make lifelong friends, experience 
					the joy of live music every night, and express myself through my art. Not to mention, I was 
					playing guitar <strong>all. the. time.</strong> 13 year old Dylan would be very proud to see the 
					life I had built. These experiences helped shape me into the person I am today. Fully ready and
					able to face anything that comes my way. It's incredibly fulfilling to have worked so hard and 
					achieve what I set out to do as a teenager just learning the guitar. The lessons were tough sometimes. 
					You play poorly, get booed, or get someone pestering you for requests. The shows were mostly good. 
				</p>
				
				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={dyl_drums}
						height={500}
						width={515}
						justify-self='center'
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						An annual highlight: <strong> Come Together Music Festival </strong>. A bi-annual music 
						festival showcasing talent from all over Canada, playing at a beautiful 1:1 scale wild 
						west village in Northern Ontario. Also I play drums sometimes!
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
				
				<p> 
					Once the Covid pandemic began, musicians weren't able to play anywhere, and thus my livelihood
					was gone. There were no shows, no rehearsals, nothing. So I was stuck working day jobs and trying 
					to figure out what I was going to do with myself. I decided to move to Nova Scotia to be closer to 
					family, and to go back to school. I thought, "Well if I can't play gigs or make music, I'd like a day job
					that is challenging and that I enjoy doing."
				</p>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image 
						src={dyl_insnow}
						width={500}
						height={500}
						alt="Walking up a snowy hill in Nova Scotia"
					/>
				</figure>

				<p> 
					In Nova Scotia, my partner pushed me to try programming. I’d always been into design, game development, 
					and how systems fit together in harmony (music pun intended). I worked through Harvard’s CS50, took pages of notes, and 
					got hooked on how computers work. That led me to apply to Nova Scotia Community College and commit to a 
					real career shift. I’d heard musicians who understand theory often make strong programmers, and enough of 
					the industry is full of musicians that it felt like a path where I could find my way.
				</p>

				<p>
					I graduated after placing 2nd in the college’s first annual hackathon, and was awarded 2024-2025 Student of 
					the Year for my role building a full-stack data-entry training app for health students. Along the way I got 
					hands-on with a wide range of languages and tools: games, screensavers, web apps, and even basic HTTP servers 
					in C. 
				</p>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={nscc_group}
						height={530}
						width={800}
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						My graduating class at Nova Scotia Community College. Your boy in the back! 
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<p>
					What I have learned from music, I apply directly to engineering. Practice, learn, listen, and keep showing up. I'm 
					at my best on collaborative teams, and I care a lot about the craft of what users actually use. I'm currently looking 
					for full-time work as a software developer. I want to keep learning fast, ship real products, and work with teams that 
					care deeply about craft. 
					
				</p> 
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.about-page {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0 0 5rem;
	}

	.about-content {
		max-width: 720px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 6vw, 6rem) 3rem;
		color: #17130f;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.about-content p {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
	}

	.about-figure {
		display: table;
		margin: 2rem auto;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.about-figure img {
		display: block;
		max-width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	.about-figure figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		color: rgba(23, 19, 15, 0.65);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-style: italic;
	}
</style>
